{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1793569484,"nonce":"iMkFU9JOM4nOsN5tyZcCJ+e/Usw=","title":"Tree view and sidebar follow ashui: rows by rule, sidebar width by CSS transition","message":"The tree view looked broken (cramped rows, Rust-coloured labels, diff glyphs, an absolute guide line offset by hand) and its open/close read oddly. The sidebar animated by FLIP: animate_bounds on the rail, every item, every title and the content wrapper, with labels removed from the tree when collapsed.\n\nPort both from ashui (TreeView.hx, Sidebar.hx, components.css .ui-tree-* / .ui-sidebar-*):\n\nTree\n- .cn-tree \u003e .cn-tree-item \u003e .cn-tree-row (+ .cn-tree-group). Row: chevron or chevron-space (14), icon (16), label. Row 28px high, 8px side padding, 6px gap; groups 14px in with 7px padding and a .cn-tree-guide line (no per-side border in the CSS parser, so a 1px absolute child coloured by rule).\n- data-selected / data-diff / data-focus-visible on rows; data-state on items and groups. All colours are rules; selected = color-mix(primary 24%).\n- Group height eases by token-timed layout animation (CSS can't transition height: auto); items carry a position animation so rows below move with it.\n- Keyboard parity with ashui after a click: Up/Down, Home/End, Right opens/enters, Left closes/parent, Enter/Space select. Pointer-focus emulation as in the gauges.\n- Guides on by default.\n\nSidebar\n- .cn-sidebar width var(--cn-sidebar-width, 200px), collapsed var(--cn-sidebar-collapsed-width, 41px), transition: width. CSS layout transitions relayout each frame, so .cn-sidebar-inset in .cn-sidebar-layout follows with no animation of its own.\n- Labels fade, group labels fold (height/padding/opacity), chevron turns, active item is data-active with the icon primary by rule.\n- expanded_width/collapsed_width were never read; removed in favour of rules. The DSL's expanded_w/collapsed_w props now forward nothing (they never did anything).\n\nChecked headless: inset edge 200,178,135,97,72,57,47,42,41 over 30ms steps; tree rows below an opening group move partway at 50ms.\n\nNot verified in a real window: 5bfc932 (tree animation freezing until the mouse moves) was about the windowed redraw loop, which the headless harness does not exercise.","files":null}]}